==Icelandic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ríða||to ride|lang=non}} from {{proto|Germanic|ridanan|lang=is}} from {{proto|Indo-European|reidh-|lang=is}}. Cognates include Old English {{term|rida||to ride|lang=ang}}, English {{term|ride|lang=en}} and German {{term|reiten|lang=de}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|reið|reiðum|riðið}}

# {{context|transitive|takes the dative|especially on horseback}} to [[ride]]{{jump|is|ride|s}}
#: ''Ekki '''ríða''' hestinum mínum.''
#:: Don't '''ride''' my horse.
#: ''Að fara '''ríðandi'''.''
#:: To '''go on''' horseback.
# {{context|ambitransitive|takes the dative|vulgar|lang=is}} to [[fuck]] someone, to [[have sex]] with{{jump|is|fuck|s}}
#: ''Langar þig að '''ríða'''?''
#:: Do you wanna '''fuck'''?
#: '''''Ríddu''' mér.''
#:: [[fuck me|'''Fuck''' me]].
#: ''Hvað er langt síðan þú hefur '''riðið'''?''
#:: How long is it since your last '''shag'''?
# {{context|lang=is|impersonal|takes the dative case}}
#: ''Fréttirnar '''riðu''' honum að fullu.''
#:: The news '''finished''' him off.
#: ''Þetta '''ríður''' á miklu.''
#:: This is '''very important'''.
# {{context|transitive|takes the accusative}} 
#: ''Ég [[ríða af sér|'''reið''' hann af mér]].''
#:: I '''rode''' fasted than he did.

=====Derived terms=====
* [[ríða á miklu]] (to be very important)
* [[ríða á vaðið]] (to [[take the first step]])
* [[ríða af]] (especially of shots and bullets; to be [[fired]])
*: ''Skotið '''reið af'''.''
*:: The shot was '''fired'''.
* [[aldan reið yfir]] (the [[wave]] broke)
* [[ríða af sér]] (+{{accusative}}, to ride away from sby, to ride faster than another)
* [[ríða að fullu]] (to [[exhaust]], to finish somebody off)
* [[ríða burtreið]] ("[[tilt]]", "[[joust]]")
* [[ríða yfir]]
* [[reið]]

=====Synonyms=====
* {{jump|s|is|ride}} [[ríða hesti]]
* {{jump|s|is|fuck}} [[hafa kynmök]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Because the word denotes both the meaning of ''riding an animal'' and ''fucking'', it is often a the subject of [[double entendre]] [[bestiality]] jokes.

